1e:["$","section",null,{"className":"mb-14","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-fg mb-6","children":"Common questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"Why does my product page get clicks but no add-to-carts?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Three causes account for most cases: price + shipping not visible before the CTA, no social proof adjacent to the buy button, and a CTA that competes with secondary actions like wishlist or compare. Each is observable in the page HTML."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"Should the price be above the fold on an ecommerce landing page?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Yes. Cold paid traffic from an ad hasn't been warmed up to price anchoring. Hiding the price (or showing it only after variant selection) adds a qualification step the visitor didn't ask for. Visible price + shipping estimate above the fold reduces the surprise at checkout."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"How many reviews do I need above the fold to improve conversion?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"One prominent aggregate (e.g., '4.8 stars · 2,340 reviews') placed directly below the product headline outperforms zero proof. The count matters more than the prose - visitors use the number as a proxy for adoption risk."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"Does product image quality affect conversion?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Directly. On mobile, a single compressed hero image with no zoom or alt-angle views forces the visitor to trust the product on one frame. High-res images with at least 3 angles, rendered above fold on mobile, reduce perceived purchase risk."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted/20 p-5","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-sm font-semibold text-fg mb-2","children":"What is the biggest CTA mistake on product pages?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg-muted leading-6","children":"Running 3-4 actions at equal visual weight - Add to Cart, Add to Wishlist, Compare, Share - so the visitor can't identify the primary action. One primary CTA, high contrast, full-width on mobile. Everything else secondary or removed."}]]}]]}]]}]
